When is the next Lady Quakers track and field event, and where will it take place? Answer according to: The Salem MS Girls Track & Field team took 3rd out of 16 teams on Friday night at Beaver Local. Rylee Hutton was the the event’s champion in both the 100m dash and the 200m dash with times of 13.97 and 28.16, respectively. Also placing in the top 4 for the Lady Quakers was Ella Double in both the 1600m (2nd) and the 800m (3rd), the 1600m relay team (4th) of Zoie Reid, Kylie Skinner, Kami Rohm and Double, the 4x200m Relay team (2nd) of Skinner, Hutton, Reid, and Bri Cibula, and the 4x100m Relay team (4th) of Ilani Jones- Wallace, Cibula, Skinner, and Annika Murray. The Lady Quakers return to action Monday at Carroll This instance will be ignored in loss calculation. Note, if this happens often, consider increasing the `max_seq_length`.
